{
  "id": "COMPOUND:17827 - PROTEIN:6149",
  "verbalization": "Ethyl 3-(methylthio)propionate is implicated in the pathway leading to the High-affinity choline transporter through a series of molecular interactions. The evidence suggests that this compound targets Thioredoxin, mitochondrial, which in turn is a target of multiple compounds, including Yuanhunine, (Salicylato-O1,O2)silver, and Rhetsinine. All of these intermediates ultimately interact with the High-affinity choline transporter, indicating a potential functional link in the cellular process of choline transport. The integration of these pathways highlights a possible role for Ethyl 3-(methylthio)propionate in modulating choline transport through its interaction with Thioredoxin, which may serve as a bridge in the metabolic network. The recurring involvement of Thioredoxin and its downstream targets suggests a conserved mechanism, though the exact functional role of Ethyl 3-(methylthio)propionate remains to be fully elucidated.",
